UPDATE companies SET description='Hacer Santa Fe operates in Santa Fe, New Mexico, as a community-oriented natural fiber and fabric studio. The founding year and founders are not publicly disclosed. The name "Hacer," Spanish for "to make" and pronounced "ah-sehr," reflects its mission to provide materials and inspiration for fiber crafting journeys.

The shop stocks a curated selection of fabrics, yarns, spinning and felting fibers, embroidery floss, and kits from brands such as Moda Fabrics, Cloud 9, Art Gallery Fabrics, Ruby Star Society, and Cosmo. Beyond retail, Hacer hosts maker groups, offers project support, and runs classes covering techniques like sashiko mending and embroidery. Facility size, headcount, and sales volumes are not disclosed.

The store serves individual crafters, knitters, sewers, and fiber artists seeking natural materials and community workspace. Its offerings cater to hobbyists and makers pursuing projects ranging from garment sewing to decorative stitching, with a focus on accessible, hands-on learning.

Hacer was founded on the belief that making and crafting can heal minds, bodies, and souls, positioning the studio as a gathering place for creative practice rather than solely a supply outlet.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabric and yarn retail", "Craft classes and workshops", "Maker community space", "Project consultation", "Sashiko instruction"], "industries": ["Arts and crafts", "Textile retail", "Fiber arts education"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Linen", "Wool", "Natural fibers", "Embroidery thread", "Sashiko thread"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Community-oriented natural fiber and fabric studio", "Offers maker groups, project support, and hands-on classes", "Curates natural fibers and fabrics from multiple independent brands", "Founded on the belief that crafting heals mind, body, and soul", "Provides sashiko mending supplies and instruction"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Hacer Santa Fe -> db", "Location: Santa Fe, New Mexico -> db", "Description: community oriented natural fiber and fabric studio -> db", "Website: hacersantafe.com -> db", "Meaning of Hacer: ''to make'' in Spanish, pronounced ''ah-sehr'' -> /", "Belief that making and crafting heal minds, bodies, souls -> /", "Offers fabrics, yarns, spinning/felting fibers, embroidery floss, kits -> /", "Hosts maker groups, project support, classes -> /", "Carries brands: Moda Fabrics, Cloud 9, Art Gallery Fabrics, Ruby Star Society, Free Spirit Fabrics, Windham, Cosmo, The Colonial Needle, Checker Distributors, Hachette Book Group, Approved Textiles, Miniature Rhino -> /", "Sells sashiko mending supplies, templates, books, kits -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Santa Fe''s community oriented natural fiber and fabric studio... providing you the materials and inspiration for your fiber crafting journey", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "exp