hing, hang tabs -> /", "Commitment to quality and innovation -> /about", "Forward-thinking, exploring new technologies and materials -> /about", "Headquarters: Fort Smith, Arkansas -> db", "Company type: Manufacturer -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Hahn Packaging manufactures quality paperboard folding cartons and set-up boxes to wholesalers, distributors and the industry.", "founded_year": "1923", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1,000 pieces", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hahn-packaging-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Haley''s Metal Shop, Inc. has operated from Biddeford, Maine since 1917. The fifth-generation family-owned business traces its roots to the Haley family, who established the shop over a century ago to serve the metalworking needs of northern New England.

The company provides custom metal fabrication, commercial and industrial sheet metal work, and commercial/industrial HVAC systems. Its fabrication shop produces ornamental details, signage, and architectural metal surfaces, while the sheet metal division handles design, engineering, fabrication, and installation for factories, commercial buildings, and geothermal projects. The HVAC side supplies ductwork, ventilation, metal roofing, and cladding for large-scale facilities.

Clients span healthcare, education, and historic preservation. Recent projects include the University of Southern Maine Center for the Arts, a neurological physical therapy suite for MaineHealth (MHMMC), and the renovation of the Franklin Block Building in Portsmouth, New Hampshire. The shop also serves commercial, industrial, and residential customers throughout Maine and New England.

