UPDATE companies SET description='Harvest Solar Energy LLC was established in 2002 in Tulsa, Oklahoma, as a family-run business by John Miggins, who installed a solar system on his own home that same year and became a recognized pioneer in the region. The company operates with a small team of dedicated professionals, including co-founders Debbie Miggins (vice president) and Matthew Miggins (owner of the exclusive installation partner Here Comes the Sun), along with partner Dalton Burgess.

The firm designs and supplies custom solar energy systems for residential and commercial clients, specializing in roof-mount, ground-mount, and off-grid configurations with battery backup. In 2023 alone, the company oversaw the installation of more than 3,000 solar panels and over 700 kWh of battery storage through its licensed install partner, Here Comes the Sun (Oklahoma license #00198075). Project sizes range from single-home arrays to larger commercial installations such as the 192-panel system at Guthrie Green and the 80-panel array at the Public Service Company of Oklahoma headquarters.

Harvest Solar serves homeowners, businesses, and public-sector customers across Oklahoma, Texas, Arkansas, and Missouri. Notable references include the Guthrie Green park project, the PSO headquarters, and numerous residential installations featuring brands such as CW Energy, QCell, Canadian Solar, Sol-Ark, Enphase, and Ruixu batteries.

The company emphasizes its family-owned structure, over two decades of solar and wind experience, and a turnkey process that begins with a free consultation and a detailed energy-savings proposal before scheduling installation with its dedicated partner crew. This approach earned Harvest Solar the Tulsa World’s “Best in the World” 2025 award for Best Solar Energy Company.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom solar system design", "Roof-mount solar installation", "Ground-mount solar installation", "Off-grid solar system design", "Battery backup system integration", "Solar consultation and energy savings analysis", "Commercial solar project development", "Residential solar installation", "Solar panel procurement", "Inverter procurement", "Battery procurement", "Generator procurement"], "industries": ["Renewable Energy", "Residential", "Commercial", "Utilities", "Public Sector"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Solar panels (CW Energy, Phono Solar, QCell, Canadian Solar)", "Solar inverters (Sol-Ark, Enphase, Fronius, SMA Sunnyboy, SolarEdge)", "Solar batteries (Ruixu, Discover, Sol-Ark)", "Generators (Briggs & Stratton, Kohler)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-run business with over 20 years of solar and wind power experience", "Exclusive licensed install partner Here Comes the Sun (OK license #00198075)", "Free consultation and detailed energy savings proposals", "Custom residential and commercial solar solutions including off-grid and battery backup"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2002 -> db", "Headquarters Tulsa, Oklahoma -> db", "Family-run business -> /about-us", "Founder John Miggins installed solar on his house in 2002 -> /about-us", "Exclusive install partner Here Comes the Sun with OK license #00198075 -> /about-us, /services", "Over 3,000 solar panels and 700 kWh battery storage installed in 2023 -> /", "Projects: Guthrie Green (192 panels), PSO Headquarters (80 panels) -> /", "Residential 