UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1969 in Houston, Texas, Houston Transformer Company, LTD. has operated as a privately held manufacturer of custom magnetic devices. The company began with a focus on wound magnetics for demanding applications and has remained headquartered in its original city.

The company designs and builds custom transformers, inductors, chokes, reactors, and coils ranging from sub-miniature surface-mount devices to three-phase units weighing over 1,500 pounds. Its 33,000-square-foot climate-controlled facility houses an on-site machine shop and sheet-metal department that produce metal bobbins, cases, NEMA-rated enclosures, and custom core configurations. The shop maintains an inventory of roughly 25,000 pounds of high-grade silicon steel to shorten cycle times, and the engineering team brings more than 75 years of combined design experience. Headcount falls in the 51-to-200 range.

Houston Transformer serves original equipment manufacturers and single-piece buyers across energy exploration, drilling operations, medical and biomedical equipment, military and aerospace programs, audio and lighting systems, data processing, industrial process control, and communications. Products have been used in downhole tools operating above 250 °C, in medical instruments, and in high-reliability defense systems.

The company emphasizes a ''can-do'' philosophy, fast prototyping, and adherence to UL and other industry standards. Its quality policy targets continuous improvement through a monitored quality management system, while its safety policy prioritizes an injury-free workplace. These commitments, along with in-house fabrication of cores and enclosures, are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom magnetic design", "Fast prototyping", "Testing (electrical, environmental)", "Traceability documentation", "UL and industry standards compliance", "Custom core configuration (toroidal, bobbin, layer wound, water-cooled, transposed windings, metal coil, self-supporting coils)", "CNC machining and machine shop services", "Sheet metal fabrication (NEMA enclosures, cases, cabinets)", "Winding with copper and aluminum conductors", "Value-added assembly", "Precision coil winding", "High-temperature magnetics (up to 450\u00b0F)", "High-voltage insulation (up to 10kV)", "High-current capacity (up to 1500A)", "Power rating up to 250 kVA"], "industries": ["Energy exploration", "Drilling operations", "Medical/biomedical", "Military", "Aerospace", "Audio", "Lighting/LEDs", "Data processing", "Industrial process control", "Communications"], "materials": ["Silicon steel (high-grade)", "Copper conductors", "Aluminum conductors", "Ferrite cores", "Steel (for enclosures)"], "equipment": ["Steel cutting equipment (in-house)", "CNC machine shop", "Sheet metal fabrication equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house steel cutting equipment for custom core configurations", "Inventory of ~25,000 lbs high-grade silicon steel to reduce cycle time", "On-site machine shop and sheet metal department for metal bobbins, cases, and NEMA enclosures", "Climate-controlled 33,000 sq ft facility with engineering staff averaging 75+ years combined experience", "Fast prototyping and UL/industry standards compliance"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 in Houston, Texas -> db, /about-us", "33,000 sq ft climate-controlled facility -> /about-us", "On-site machine shop and sheet metal department -> /about-us, /services, /capabilities", "Inventory of ~25,000 lbs silicon steel -> /capabilities", "Engineering staff with 75+ years combined experience -> /about-us", "Headcount 51-200 -> db", "Industries served: energy exploration, drilling, medical, military, aerospace, audio, lighting, data processing, industrial process control, communications -> db industries_served", "Products sold in single piece quantities and to OEMs -> /", "Custom core configurations: toroidal, bobbin, layer wound, water-cooled, transposed windings, metal coil, self-supporting coils -> /services, /capabilities", "UL and industry standards compliance -> /services, /capabilities", "Fast prototyping -> /services", "Quality management system and safety policy -> /quality", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom transformer, inductor, and magnetic-device manufacturer headquartered and manufacturing in Houston, Texas.", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "51-200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 piece", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/houston-transformer-company-ltd/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='houston-transformer-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Howard Industries, headquartered in Ellisville, Mississippi, was founded in 1969. The firm is led by principal Peter Howard, who established the company to invest in and support management teams building market-businesses.

The company operates as a private investment firm, using its own capital to acquire and partner with small and medium-sized manufacturers and specialized service businesses. Its portfolio has included companies in motor and gear production, specialty plastics, data center infrastructure, powder coating, fan and blower manufacturing, digital asset tracking, and label production.

Howard Industries targets niche manufacturers and service providers with defensible market positions, typically with earnings between $1 million and $6 million. It has invested in businesses across the United States, Mexico, China, and the United Kingdom, spanning sectors such as steel processing, textiles, tubing, electrical components, and data center services.

The firm emphasizes long-term partnerships over quick returns, citing certainty of close due to using its own capital, candid communication, and a focus on incremental operational improvement. It seeks companies with proprietary processes, product innovation, or strong customer relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Private equity investment", "Portfolio company strategic support", "Operational improvement consulting", "Add-on acquisitions", "Turnaround management"], "industries": ["Steel processing", "Textiles", "Tubing", "Electrical components", "Motor and gear manufacturing", "Specialty plastics", "Data center infrastructure", "Powder coating", "Fan and blower manufacturing", "Digital asset tracking", "Bar code and RF labels", "Hinges and hardware", "Consoles and racks", "Distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Uses its own capital for high certainty to close", "No pressure to sell dictated by outside partners", "Candid communication builds trust with partners", "Focus on long-term development rather than quick returns", "Supports management through incremental improvement and analytics"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 -> db", "Headquarters Ellisville, Mississippi -> db", "Principal Peter Howard -> /", "Private investment firm using own capital -> /", "Portfolio includes Jakel, Inc., Continental Structural Plastics, Critical Facilities Solutions, CPCS, Comair Rotron, EnaSys, Rug Barn, Colorflex/TTG, Lawrence Manufacturing, e-Systems Group, EDP Europe -> /", "Investment criteria: earnings $1M-$6M -> /", "Address 1850 Lefthand Circle, Longmont, CO -> /", "25+ years of investing -> /", "$400 million invested -> /", "16 investments -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Howard Industries was founded to invest in and support management teams to build market-leading businesses.", "founded_year": "1969", "employee_count": "", 