UPDATE companies SET description='Hubco Inc. operates from Hutchinson, Kansas, where it was founded in 1919 as the Hutchinson Bag Company by Emerson Carey and James Dick. The business began manufacturing bags for the salt industry and has remained in continuous operation for over a century.

Today the company produces a range of textile bags including cotton, burlap, and specialty fabrics. Its product line covers geological sample bags for mining and oil exploration, agricultural bags, cathodic protection and anode bags, retail and specialty packaging, tea towels, and food-grade packaging. Hubco also offers custom letterpress printing and an online bag builder for tailored designs, emphasizing American-made production and the ability to fulfill small orders.

Customers span mining, oil and gas, agriculture, food processing, and retail sectors. Long-term clients include Origin Utensils, Whiskey Leatherworks, Oklahoma State University’s soil lab, Garber Farms, and Farmaceuticals International, all of whom cite consistent quality and responsive service.

Hubco distinguishes itself through domestic manufacturing, quick turnaround on custom orders, and a focus on personal customer relationships. The company states that its commitment to quality products and exemplary customer service has allowed it to thrive while competitors have shifted to imported goods.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Textile bag manufacturing (cotton, burlap, specialty fabrics)", "Geological sample bag production", "Agricultural bag production", "Cathodic protection/anode bag production", "Retail and specialty packaging", "Tea towel and fabric production", "Food packaging manufacturing", "Custom letterpress printing", "Custom bag design via online builder", "Envelope and carton manufacturing"], "industries": ["Mining", "Oil exploration", "Agriculture", "Food packaging", "Retail", "Geological sampling"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Burlap (jute)", "Specialty fabrics", "Paper (envelopes and cartons)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made textile bags", "Custom letterpress printing", "Accepts small orders", "Online bag builder for custom designs", "Responsive customer service"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1919 by Emerson Carey and James Dick as Hutchinson Bag Company -> /", "Headquarters in Hutchinson, Kansas -> db", "Manufactures textile bags (cotton, burlap, geological, agricultural, cathodic protection, retail, specialty, tea towels, food packaging) -> /", "Offers custom letterpress printing and online bag builder -> /", "Serves mining, oil exploration, agriculture, food packaging, retail, geological sampling -> /", "Customer examples: Origin Utensils, Whiskey Leatherworks, Oklahoma State University Soil Lab, Garber Farms, Farmaceuticals International -> /", "Differentiators: American-made, small orders, responsive service -> /", "Materials: cotton, burlap (jute), specialty fabrics, paper -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our main focus as a textile bag manufacturer and supplier is to provide our clients with custom cotton, burlap, and other textile bags.", "founded_year": "1919", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/hubcoinc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='hubco-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huerta Furniture is a family-run custom furniture maker based in Arcadia, California, founded in 1996. The company began as a family operation serving Southern California with handmade, made-in-USA furniture.

The shop produces custom sofas, sectionals, chaise loungers, pull-out beds, armchairs, and daybeds, each customizable down to leg style, button spacing, and nail-head patterns. A design team assists clients through fabric selection from hundreds of warehouse samples and foam choices including standard, memory foam, and feather-down options. All pieces are fabricated in-house and delivered throughout Southern California.

The company serves residential customers across Southern California, with reviewers located in Los Angeles, Norwalk, and South El Monte. Clients include homeowners seeking tailored seating for living rooms and apartments, as well as those needing quick turnaround for events.

Huerta Furniture emphasizes honest craftsmanship, hospitable service, and unbeatable value, promising completed custom pieces within two weeks. The family ownership model drives a no-pressure design process where customers can redesign until satisfied, and pricing is positioned as unmatched for the caliber of custom work.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Upholstery", "Foam selection (standard, memory foam, feather down)", "Fabric selection", "Furniture fabrication", "Delivery and installation"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom furniture"], "materials": ["Fabric", "Foam (standard, memory foam, feather down)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "2 weeks for custom orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom furniture delivered in two weeks", "Hundreds of fabric samples in warehouse", "Family-run with honest craftsmanship", "No-pressure design process with unlimited revisions", "Unmatched pricing for custom caliber"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Family-run -> db", "Headquarters Arcadia, California -> db", "Custom furniture making business -> /", "Serves Southern California -> /", "Handmade, made in USA -> /", "Products: sofas, sectionals, chaise loungers, pull-out beds, armchairs, daybeds -> /", "Customizable details: leg style, button spacing, nail heads -> /", "Design team assists with fabric and foam selection -> /", "Hundreds of fabric options in warehouse -> /", "Foam types: standard, memory foam, feather down -> /", "Two-week turnaround for custom orders -> /", "Unmatched pricing for custom caliber -> /", "No-pressure design process -> /", "Customer reviews from Los Angeles, Norwalk, South El Monte -> /", "Address: 1550 Clark St, Arcadia CA 91006 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Huerta Furniture is a family-run custom furniture making business serving all of Southern California since 1996.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='huerta-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Husky Technologies, headquartered in Milton, Vermont, was founded in 1953. The company began as a provider of injection molding systems and has grown into a global supplier of equipment and services for the plastics industry.

The company designs and manufactures complete injection molding systems, including hot runners, mold controllers, and proactive monitoring services. Its product lineup comprises specialized platforms such as the HyPET®6e and HyPET® NX6 for PET preform production, the ICHOR system for precision syringe and medical device molding, the HyCAP™4 for high-performance closure molding, the HyPERSYNC™ for food container molding, and the HyLECTRIC® for high-performance packaging. Husky supports customers in more than 140 countries through a worldwide network that delivers local installation, training, and ongoing technical support.

Husky serves beverage producers, packaging manufacturers, consumer goods brands, medical and pharmaceutical companies, and electronics manufacturers. Its systems are used for PET preform and bottle production, thin-wall food containers, beverage and specialty closures, medical devices such as syringes, and electronic components.

The company distinguishes itself by positioning as a technology partner rather than a machine supplier, offering the Husky Advantage+Elite™ service that provides real-time proactive, predictive, and transparent equipment monitoring. This service includes extended protection plans, machine audits, refurbishments, and upgrades aimed at minimizing unplanned downtime and lowering part costs over the life of the system.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding system design and manufacturing", "Hot runner systems", "Mold controllers", "Proactive monitoring services (Husky Advantage+Elite\u2122)", "Equipment installation and training", "Real-time predictive equipment monitoring", "OEM parts supply", "Technical assistance and troubleshooting", "Maintenance and protection plans", "Machine audits", "Equipment refurbishment", "System upgrades", "PET preform molding systems", "Medical device molding systems", "Closure molding systems", "Food container molding systems", "Packaging molding systems"], "industries": ["PET preform and bottle production", "Food packaging", "Consumer goods", "Medical device manufacturing", "Beverage production", "Packaging manufacturing", "Healthcare", "Electronics manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["HyPET\u00ae6e", "HyPET\u00ae NX6", "ICHOR", "HyCAP\u21224", "HyPERSYNC\u2122", "HyLECTRIC\u00ae"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Real-time proactive, predictive, and transparent equipment monitoring via Husky Advantage+Elite\u2122", "Global support network in over 140 countries with local installation and training", "Genuine OEM parts supply, technical assistance, and troubleshooting", "Extended protection plans, machine audits, refurbishments, and upgrades", "Specialized injection molding platforms for PET, medical, closure, food container, and packaging applications"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1953 -> db", "Headquartered in Milton, Vermont -> db", "Global provider of injection molding systems, hot runners, mold controllers, proactive monitoring services -> db, /", "Specializes in PET preform and bottle production, food packaging, consumer goods, medical device manufacturing -> db, /", "Supports customers in more than 140 countries -> /", "Worldwide network enables local support -> /", "Product systems: HyPET\u00ae6e, HyPET\u00ae NX6, ICHOR, HyCAP\u21224, HyPERSYNC\u2122, HyLECTRIC\u00ae -> /", "Services: Husky Advantage+Elite\u2122 proactive monitoring, OEM parts, technical assistance, maintenance plans, machine audits, refurbishments, upgrades -> /", "Serves beverage producers, packaging manufacturers, consumer goods brands, medical/pharmaceutical, electronics -> /", "Applications: PET preform/bottle, thin-wall food containers, closures, medical devices, electronic components -> /", "Differentiator: technology partner, intelligent networks, sustainability, foresight -> /", "Contact phone  -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Husky is a global provider of injection molding systems, hot runners, mold controllers, and proactive monitoring services", "founded_year": "1953", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='husky-injection-molding-system' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huston & Company, based in Arundel, Maine, with a showroom and workshop in nearby Kennebunkport, was founded in 1988. It began with a mission to design and build furniture that integrates function, form, and master-level craftsmanship in an elegant, enduring style.

The firm produces custom hardwood furniture for residential, corporate, academic, library, and institutional settings. A select group of master craftsmen builds each piece by hand using traditional joinery—hand-cut dovetails and mortise-and-tenon joints—applied to premium hardwoods, followed by hand-rubbed finishes. Every piece is signed and dated. The workshop operates adjacent to the Kennebunkport showroom, and output is built to order, one piece at a time, with shop drawings provided for custom projects.

Clients range from individual homeowners to architects and designers specifying furnishings for university libraries, law offices, and corporate environments. The company collaborates directly with project teams to determine furnishing needs and create pieces that meet specific functional and aesthetic requirements.

Huston & Company distinguishes itself through its commitment to traditional craftsmanship, premium materials, and a design process that emphasizes wood selection, joinery, and finish—details the company says are absent from mass-produced furniture. Its founding mission centers on integrating function, form, and master-level craftsmanship into graceful, enduring pieces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Furniture", "Residential Furniture", "Institutional Furnishings", "Hand-Cut Dovetails", "Mortise and Tenon Joinery", "Hand-Rubbed Finishes", "Shop Drawings"], "industries": ["Residential", "Academic", "Library", "Corporate", "Institutional"], "materials": ["Premium hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-cut dovetail and mortise-and-tenon joinery on every piece", "Hand-rubbed finishes applied to premium hardwoods", "Each piece signed and dated by the maker", "Built to order, one at a time, with shop drawings for custom work", "Collaborative design process with architects and institutional clients"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Arundel, Maine -> db", "Showroom and workshop in Kennebunkport, Maine -> /about", "Produces custom hardwood furniture for residential, corporate, academic, library, and institutional markets -> /about, db", "Uses hand-cut dovetails and mortise-and-tenon joinery -> /about, db", "Applies hand-rubbed finishes to premium hardwoods -> /about", "Each piece signed and dated by the maker -> /about", "Built to order, one piece at a time -> /about", "Provides shop drawings for custom projects -> /about, db", "Collaborates with architects, designers, and institutional decision makers -> /about", "Serves academic, library, corporate, and residential clients -> db, /about", "Founding mission: integrate function, form, and master-level craftsmanship -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Huston & Company designs and builds all types of hardwood furniture: residential furniture for every room in the house, as well as corporate, office, library, academic and institutional furnishings.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='huston-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Huston Solar operates from Lafayette, Indiana, as a division of Huston Electric Inc., a family-owned electrical contractor founded in 1939. Now in its fourth generation of family ownership, the company began as a traditional electrical service provider and expanded into renewable energy with the creation of its solar division. Huston Electric has served central Indiana for over 80 years across five specialized divisions including electrical, signage, technology, generators, and solar.

The solar division functions as a turn-key developer and installer, managing every phase from design and permitting to utility interconnection agreements and final commissioning. The company also provides ongoing maintenance services for existing installations and assists customers with financing options such as $0 down programs and federal tax credit navigation.

Huston Solar serves a broad cross-section of central Indiana: homeowners, businesses, industrial complexes, and institutions including schools, hospitals, warehouses, and commercial campuses. Project examples cited include a kilowatt-scale roof-mount system with energy storage in Anderson and installations for various commercial and institutional clients throughout the region.

The company states its mission is to make customers'' lives easier through turnkey solutions in electrical, technology, alternative energy, and visual communications, guided by core values of safety, ownership, service, leadership, and relationship-building. Its 2025 Solar Games Championship win at Intersolar North America is presented as external validation of installation craftsmanship and team expertise.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "Industrial solar panel installation", "Solar energy storage system installation", "Solar system design and engineering", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "Solar system maintenance and service", "Roof-mount solar installation", "Ground-mount solar installation", "Federal tax credit and incentive consulting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Institutional (education, healthcare)", "Agricultural", "Government"], "materials": ["Solar modules", "Inverters", "Racking and mounting hardware", "Energy storage batteries"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turn-key solar developer and installer handling permitting and interconnection", "24/7 live-person service for the lifetime of the system", "Family-owned since 1939, now fourth generation", "IBEW Local 668 trained electricians on every installation", "2025 Solar Games Championship winner"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1939 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Lafayette, Indiana -> db, /", "Family-owned, fourth generation -> /about", "Division of Huston Electric Inc. -> /, /about", "Turn-key solar developer and installer -> /about", "IBEW Local 668 electricians -> /", "24/7 live person service -> /", "Residential, commercial, industrial, institutional clients -> /, /about", "2025 Solar Games Championship -> /", "Handles permitting and interconnection agreements -> /about", "$0 down financing options -> 