UPDATE companies SET description='Interconnect Cable Technologies Corporation (ICTC) was founded in 1988 in Brooksville, Florida, where it maintains its corporate headquarters. The company began as a specialist in low-volume, high-mix cable and wire-harness assemblies for original equipment manufacturers worldwide.

Operations span four facilities—Brooksville and Titusville in Florida, Laguna in the Philippines, and Dongguan in China—allowing a hybrid model that pairs U.S.-based precision and IP protection with high-volume offshore capacity. The company manages the entire value stream from circuit card assembly and machining through final box-build test and integration.

Customers come from aerospace and defense (aircraft wiring harnesses inspected to AS9102, Mil-Spec cable assemblies for military platforms), medical (PCBAs, cables, and harnesses built under ISO 13485, including handicap mobility products), transportation (video security and fleet management systems for public transit, embedded data collection for roadway infrastructure), industrial machinery (precision metal components, robotics, vision systems), and datacom/telecom (molded networking and power cables, electro-mechanical box builds).

ICTC says its differentiation lies in a vertically integrated, globally distributed model that simplifies supply chain complexity: domestic final assembly for compliance-critical builds, strategic labor balancing across regions, Kanban inventory solutions, tariff navigation, and reshoring support. The company’s stated mission is to simplify supply chain and manufacturing challenges, aiming to be the most trusted, friendly, and flexible contract manufacturer.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','UL','IPC/WHMA-A-620','ITAR','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cable & wire harness assembly", "PCB assembly (SMT, through-hole, component placement)", "Electronic box build integration", "Precision machining", "Turnkey assembly services", "Global supply chain management", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) support", "First article qualification (AS9102)", "Serialization (bar-coding, date stamping)", "100% electrical testing (ICT, functional)", "Dye pull testing", "Flying probe testing", "Microsectioning analysis", "Salt fog testing", "Custom drawing updates", "Offshore assembly (Philippines, China)", "Domestic final assembly", "Multi-location engineering collaboration", "Tariff navigation and compliance assistance", "Kanban inventory solutions"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Military & Defense", "Medical / Health Care", "Transportation / Transportation Safety", "Industrial / Industrial Machinery", "Datacom / Telecom"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low-volume high-mix to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hybrid domestic/global manufacturing model with U.S. IP protection and offshore cost efficiency", "Vertically integrated: circuit card assembly, precision machining, and box build under one roof", "Domestic final assembly for compliance-critical (ITAR, defense) builds", "Kanban inventory and reduced lead times through global sourcing strategies", "Reshoring support and t