UPDATE companies SET description='ITW Food Equipment Group is headquartered in Troy, Ohio, and traces its roots to 1830 when the Bonnet brand began designing, manufacturing, and installing professional kitchen equipment in Europe. The group operates as a division of Illinois Tool Works (ITW), bringing together a family of premium brands that have served foodservice and food retail professionals for over a century.

The company designs and manufactures a broad range of commercial cooking, refrigeration, warewashing, and bakery equipment under brands including Hobart, Traulsen, Baxter, Vulcan, Wolf, Stero, Foster, and Bonnet. Its innovation pipeline has produced nearly 600 ENERGY STAR® certified products, driven by more than 1,000 staff members who hold at least one invention and a 70% patent commercialization rate reported in 2013. A service network of nearly 200 offices and 1,500 factory-trained technicians covers 95% of customers within 50 miles, complemented by the SmartConnect365 remote-monitoring platform.

Wholesale and production bakery suppliers also rely on its equipment for high-volume operations.

The group emphasizes customer-driven innovation and sustainable leadership, earning the U.S. EPA’s ENERGY STAR Partner of the Year award every year since 2008 and the Sustained Excellence Award in 2024. Brands such as Foster have achieved the Carbon Trust Standard for carbon reduction, while technologies like Hobart’s Advansys energy recovery system cut energy costs by up to 50% and water use by 90% in dishwashing.', certifications=ARRAY['ENERGY STAR','Carbon Trust Standard']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial cooking equipment manufacturing", "Commercial refrigeration manufacturing", "Warewashing equipment manufacturing", "Bakery equipment manufacturing", "Equipment installation", "Preventive maintenance and repair service", "Remote equipment monitoring (SmartConnect365)", "Energy recovery systems (Advansys)", "Finless condenser coil technology", "Deliming systems for dishwashers", "Infrared cooking technology", "FivePass heat transfer system", "Full cleaning systems for ovens", "Thermal break and hot gas door heater technology"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Food retail", "Bakery (wholesale/production)", "Institutional catering (restaurants, hotels, schools, healthcare)", "Commercial kitchen equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Traulsen solid-door R & A Series", "Traulsen G-Series", "Vulcan PowerFry5", "Bonnet Precisio Oven", "Hobart Advansys Energy Recovery System", "Foster EcoPro Cabinets", "SmartConnect365 platform"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ENERGY STAR Partner of the Year every year since 2008; Sustained Excellence Award in 2024", "Nearly 600 ENERGY STAR certified products across brands", "Service network within 50 miles of 95% of customers with 200 offices and 1,500 factory-trained technicians", "Over 1,000 staff members with at least one invention; 70% patent commercialization rate (2013)", "SmartConnect365 remote monitoring and data analytics platform"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Troy, Ohio