UPDATE companies SET description='Icon Modern was founded in 2007 in Chicago, Illinois, by Rocky Levy and Aaron Tvrdy. The pair met after Levy read a Chicago Tribune article about thousands of urban trees being removed due to disease; drawing on his background in commercial furniture, he envisioned turning that waste into sustainable furniture.

The company operates as a full-service custom fabricator, producing conference tables, community tables, reception desks, space dividers, ceiling elements, feature walls, planters, and countertops. A team of architects, designers, and project managers handles engineering, value engineering, shop drawings, 3D renderings, and prototyping, overseeing each project from concept through installation.

Past clients include Starbucks, Whole Foods, Twitter, Caterpillar, IPG, and Jump Trading, with projects ranging from boardroom tables with integrated power to large-scale ceiling installations and moss walls.

